<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shandong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shandong is a coastal province of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>, with its capital at Jinan. In antiquity it was the land of the states of Qi and Lu, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confucius">Confucius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mencius">Mencius</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-tai">Mount Tai</a> there was China's most sacred mountain. A densely populated farming region, it was a German sphere of influence around Qingdao from 1898 to 1914 and is now one of China's largest provincial economies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shandong.jpg" alt="Shandong" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chrishcn · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PenglaiPavilion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
